course: dictionary
lesson: 9702
title: Sulfide: when elements join
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A sulfide is a compound made when sulfur joins with another element, often a metal. A compound is a new substance made from two or more elements that have joined together, so it is not just a mixture. «The scaly-foot snail has a shell and scales made of iron sulfide.» Here iron and sulfur have joined to make a new material.
explain: In a science lesson, you can heat iron and sulfur together to make iron sulfide. A magnet pulls iron, but it cannot pull the iron back out of iron sulfide, because the two have joined and are no longer separate. That is how you can tell a compound from a mixture.
explain: When you see sulfide in the name of a chemical, such as iron sulfide or hydrogen sulfide, you know that sulfur is part of it. Sulfide is spelled sulphide in UK books, and both spellings mean the same thing.
fact: A sulfide is a compound of sulfur joined with another element.
fact: «Iron sulfide» is made when iron and sulfur are heated together.
fact: Hydrogen sulfide is a gas that smells of rotten eggs, and it is poisonous in large amounts.
fact: «Pyrite», also called fool's gold, is iron sulfide.
fact: Many sulfides are minerals and metal ores, which are rocks that metal can be taken from.
exercise: What is a sulfide? | *A compound made of sulfur joined with another element | A gas that is always safe to breathe | A kind of magnet | A metal made of pure gold
exercise: In «The scaly-foot snail has a shell and scales made of iron sulfide», which two elements are joined? | Snail and shell | Iron and gold | Sulfur and oxygen | *Iron and sulfur
exercise: Hydrogen sulfide is a gas that smells of what? | Fresh flowers | *Rotten eggs | Burnt toast | Sweet sugar
test: Why can a magnet not pull iron out of iron sulfide? | Iron sulfide is only a mixture | Magnets only work on wood | *Iron and sulfur have joined into a new compound | Iron sulfide is too hot to touch
test: Which name is another name for fool's gold? | *Pyrite | Sulfur dioxide | Hydrogen sulfide | Iron oxide
exam: Which of these is a sulfide? | *Iron sulfide | Oxygen | Water | Sugar
